# openjdk-25-jre-headless — #7 predicted Java's JRE/JDK layer would be
# "env — easy" (JAVA_HOME + PATH), assuming the *install* succeeds. It
# doesn't: java-common's and this package's own postinst both do
# `mkdir -m 755 /etc/.java` unconditionally, unguarded by `|| true` — a
# genuine root-only write, `dpkg --configure` fails outright. Unlike
# py3compile there's no safe shim target: the failing call is a bare `mkdir`
# against an absolute /etc path, and shimming `mkdir`/`touch` globally on
# PATH would intercept every unrelated script that calls them — nowhere
# near as narrow as shimming one named debhelper tool.
#
# The apt route is a dead end here; `tools/deb2home.sh` is the actual fix —
# it extracts the .deb's files with `dpkg -x` and never runs postinst at
# all:
#
#   tools/deb2home.sh openjdk-25-jre-headless
#
# Verified: java runs with no /etc/.java present on the host at all (the
# JVM creates its Preferences-API cache lazily if missing — the postinst's
# mkdir is defensive boilerplate, not a hard runtime requirement).
#
# CAVEAT: "openjdk-25" is Debian's *current* default JDK; the package name
# and JAVA_HOME path are version-pinned like pmarkdown's PERL5LIB triplet —
# regenerate both when the default JDK version moves. deb2home.sh installs
# under $PREFIX/opt/<pkg>/, not $PREFIX/usr/ like an apt-installed package.
package  openjdk-25-jre-headless
install  unlikely
mechanism  env
env      JAVA_HOME=$PREFIX/opt/openjdk-25-jre-headless/usr/lib/jvm/java-25-openjdk-amd64
verify   $JAVA_HOME/bin/java -version
note     apt route is a dead end (root-only /etc/.java postinst, no safe shim target); install via `tools/deb2home.sh openjdk-25-jre-headless` instead — see #7
